    "what-changed-text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Price held nearly flat at $0.0000191483 (−1.1% over 24h), but the order flow underneath turned clearly bullish: 193 buys against 113 sells pushed the buy/sell ratio to 1.71, up sharply from yesterday's 1.08, on volume running 2.75× the 7-day average ($162.5K vs a $59.0K average). Whale activity (≥$1K) nearly doubled to 44 trades, split 26 buys to 18 sells — net accumulation. Yet the three largest single prints were all sells — sell $7.5K @ $0.0000174 · 11:06 UTC, sell $6.4K @ $0.0000174 · 10:16 UTC, sell $5.2K @ $0.0000184 · 10:14 UTC — which is why heavier buy-side participation didn't translate into a price pop. Liquidity ticked up slightly (+0.7% to $423.1K), ruling out a pool drain as the explanation for the stalled price.",
